From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:07:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 38/47] feat(telemetry): render trial reports, forwarded to an
 OpenTelemetry collector

The canvas has two render experiments behind switches (the GPU picture
layer and zoom pictures). Whether they help depends on the device, so the
editor is about to measure them per browser; this is where the
measurements go. POST /api/telemetry/render takes one small JSON report
from the browser: which level of each experiment it had and why, its
device class, and frame counts and timings per kind of camera gesture.

The route
- validates against a closed zod schema (shared/renderTrialSchema.ts, apart
  from the vocabulary in shared/renderTrial.ts so the editor's bundle does
  not carry zod): enums,
  bounded numbers, a renderer string of printable ASCII up to 80
  characters, at most 8 rows, unknown keys refused. Nothing in it names a
  user, canvas, frame or address, and the schema cannot carry one;
- caps the body at 8 KB with its own parser, ahead of the 10 MB one, and
  answers 413/400 itself instead of Express's HTML error page;
- sits ahead of the /api gate, which keeps a share-link guest to its
  canvas routes: any session may report (account, link guest, embedded
  panel), no session gets 401, a cross-site request 403;
- answers 204 for a valid report, also past the rate limit (30 per ten
  minutes per session user, the in-memory sliding window the import and
  sync limits use) and for an impersonating admin, whose reports are
  dropped: the browser has nothing to retry and nothing to show.

Forwarding
When OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT is set, each report goes to
<endpoint>/v1/logs as OTLP/HTTP JSON logs, one INFO record per row with
the body "render trial" and flat doop.render.* attributes (arm A-D,
levels and reasons, gesture kind/stratum/live, frames, slow frames, slow
share, mean and p95 interval, device class, current verdicts), so a log
query can sum frames and slow frames by arm without unpacking a body.
Rows count only what was measured since the page's previous report, so
sums across reports count each frame once. Resource attributes follow
the SDK variables: OTEL_SERVICE_NAME (default doop, and it wins over a
service.name in the list) plus OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES (k=v,k=v,
percent-decoded). Plain fetch with a 3 s timeout, after the response;
failures are swallowed with one warning per ten minutes. Unset, a report
is validated and dropped. The OpenTelemetry JS SDK was ruled out: one
record type a few times per page load does not need a dependency, a
batcher or a provider.

Tests: tests/telemetry.test.ts (validation and garbage, 413, no session,
cross-site, a guest allowed, rate limit, impersonation, the drop when
unset, the exact OTLP body against a local HTTP collector, resource
attributes, a failing collector warning once).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
